+# R1's run plan: Thursday 3 December 2026
+
+The first VM day of the netcode proof test (u8-brief.md rev 1.1 section 6, with the advisor's C1, C3, C6, C7, C8 and
+L1-L3; plan.md §7.2-§7.3 as NPT-TRIM trims them). Mustafa OKs this plan, its cap (EUR 0.80) and its delete-by times at
+Stop B (Tuesday 1 December), before any VM exists. Every laptop reading in it is **rough, not judged; R8 judges the
+seven marks (-1, -14, -28, -29, -36, PM-0006-16, PM-0006-25) once he names the laptop** (LAPTOP (b)).
+
+**Condition 2's line** (advisor-u6a-brief.md:233-237, word for word): "Until U6d merges, U6a's, U6b's, U6c's, U7's and
+U8's briefs and R1's run plan each state in one line that their tests or runs hold no throwing or rejoining hostile
+client and no client restarted mid-run, or bring C-U6-19 first. In R1 each browser leg (each browser on each
+transport, the QUIC-blocked fallback, -36's three) joins its own slot once, or the room restarts between legs; the
+token file holds a slot for every leg. SA-F1-1 stays open until U6d merges."
+**R1's line:** R1's runs hold no throwing or rejoining hostile client and no client restarted mid-run: every browser
+attempt joins its own slot once (section 4), and LG's bots join once per room.
+
+**The commit pair** (the brief's choice 2): rs.yaml and lg.yaml name the run's code commit Y (`/etc/npt/commit`); they
+live at X = Y plus that line. He pastes the Cloud config from
+`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Mergincanli/Shamble-Frontlines/<X>/spikes/netcode-proof/ops/cloud-init/rs.yaml`
+(and `lg.yaml`), X filled at Stop B. The user-data check compares each VM's stored file with X's; `npt-userdata head`
+on each VM must show Y for both clones.
+
+## 1. Blocks and hours
+C1: Manual mode prompts every laptop command and no ssh allow exists, so while he is away the laptop runs nothing. A
+block marked away is started by cloud-init or by one `r1.sh chain` prompt given before he leaves; it runs on RS,
+detached, holding its rooms' stdin itself, and writes a done or stopped marker that the session reads when he is back.
+
+| Block | Hours | Marks or checks | He is | Started by |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Bring-up: cloud-init's build, the dist, the binaries | 0.60 | the build (plan.md:1175-1176) | away | cloud-init |
+| Bring-up: first commands, LG's key, `npt-ctl peers`, `r1.sh bringup` (C5, `npt-ctl cpus`, `alone`) | 0.30 | condition 4, C-U8-1, C5; -16 | present | laptop |
+| Certificate: staging, then production (two TXT records) | 0.25 | the WebSocket leg's trusted name | present | laptop |
+| Headers | 0.15 | -1, -2, PM-0006-11, -16 | away | chain server |
+| L2 probe with ImpairSocket's self-test (0 added hours) | 0.20 | -3; conditions C-U8-2, C-U8-4, C-U8-6 | away | chain server |
+| Calibration | 0.10 | load spread; -16 | away | chain server |
+| Room starts | 0.10 | -16 | away | chain server |
+| DelayStream's loaded self-test | 0.15 | condition 10 (C-U8-3, -5); -16 | away | chain server |
+| S14 veth and netem check | 0.80 | TCP-FREEZE | away | chain server |
+| Four-browser smoke, both transports | 0.25 | -14 (rough), -56's item 2 | present | laptop |
+| Dev certificate pinned by hash in every browser | 0.20 | PM-0006-25 (rough) | present | laptop |
+| QUIC-blocked fallback, four browsers | 0.25 | -29 (rough) | present | laptop |
+| Ping, laptop and PC | 0.10 | PM-0006-12 | present | laptop |
+| -36's home EU path, three browsers at once | 0.50 | -36 (rough) | present | laptop |
+| First bites | 0.10 | the R1 bites | present | chain bites |
+| **Planned** | **3.55** | billed 4 per VM | | |
+
+Arithmetic: plan.md:819's 2.95 less Safari's 0.30 is 2.65; plus -29's 0.25 and PM-0006-25's 0.20 is 3.10; plus
+DelayStream's 0.15 and S14's 0.30 is **3.55**, inside the 4 billed hours. The slack is per VM, against its
+delete-by (INF-SB-7): RS's 13:30 less teardown's end 13:25 is **5 minutes** at worst (25 if RS goes first in the
+teardown), LG's about 13:20 less its deletion at about 13:10 about 10 minutes. S14 then grows to 0.80 h
+(NC-SB-4: three runs of 950 s, a 600 s steady window and 34 bursts each, about 48 minutes with set-up) and stays the
+server chain's last block, so its last **0.50 h** runs beside the browser legs: the rows sum to 4.05 and the day's
